37
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:47,119
Preface

38
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:49,119
About 10 years ago, while spending a few

39
00:01:47,119 --> 00:01:51,040
days under the hospitable roof of the

40
00:01:49,119 --> 00:01:54,399
distinguished Belgian jurist, the

41
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:56,960
lamented Msure de La, our conversation

42
00:01:54,399 --> 00:02:00,399
turned during one of our rambles to the

43
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:03,119
subject of religion. Do you mean to say,

44
00:02:00,399 --> 00:02:05,280
asked the venerable professor, that you

45
00:02:03,119 --> 00:02:06,799
have no religious instruction in your

46
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:08,800
schools?

47
00:02:06,799 --> 00:02:11,280
On my replying in the negative, he

48
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:13,599
suddenly halted in astonishment, and in

49
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:16,959
a voice which I shall not easily forget,

50
00:02:13,599 --> 00:02:20,800
he repeated, "No religion,

51
00:02:16,959 --> 00:02:23,200
how do you impart moral education?"

52
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:24,959
The question stunned me at the time. I

53
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:27,120
could give no ready answer, for the

54
00:02:24,959 --> 00:02:30,000
moral precepts I learned in my childhood

55
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:32,319
days were not given in schools. And not

56
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,560
until I began to analyze the different

57
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:37,040
elements that formed my notions of right

58
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:39,040
and wrong did I find that it was

59
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:42,160
Bushidto that breathed them into my

60
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:44,000
nostrils. The direct inception of this

61
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:46,480
little book is due to the frequent

62
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,879
queries put by my wife as to the reasons

63
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:52,239
why such and such ideas and customs

64
00:02:48,879 --> 00:02:55,440
prevail in Japan. In my attempts to give

65
00:02:52,239 --> 00:02:57,680
satisfactory replies to Miss Yoda and to

66
00:02:55,440 --> 00:03:00,480
my wife, I found that without

67
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:02,560
understanding feudalism and Bushido, the

68
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:05,200
moral ideas of present Japan are a

69
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:07,440
sealed volume. Taken advantage of

70
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:09,840
enforced idleness on account of long

71
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:11,760
illness, I put down in the order now

72
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:13,360
presented to the public some of the

73
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:16,000
answers given in our household

74
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:17,760
conversation. They consist mainly of

75
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
what I was taught and told in my

76
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:23,200
youthful days when feudalism was still

77
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,080
in force. Between LaCardio Hearn and

78
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:28,720
Mrs. Hugh Fraser on one side and Sir

79
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:31,440
Ernest Sato and Professor Chamberlain on

80
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:34,319
the other, it is indeed discouraging to

81
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:36,799
write anything Japanese in English. The

82
00:03:34,319 --> 00:03:39,120
only advantage I have over them is that

83
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:41,360
I can assume the attitude of a personal

84
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:43,680
defendant, while these distinguished

85
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:45,280
writers are at best solicitors and

86
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:48,159
attorneys.

87
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:50,239
I have often thought, had I their gift

88
00:03:48,159 --> 00:03:53,760
of language, I would present the cause

89
00:03:50,239 --> 00:03:55,760
of Japan in more eloquent terms. But one

90
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:58,159
who speaks in a borrowed tongue should

91
00:03:55,760 --> 00:04:00,080
be thankful if he can just make himself

92
00:03:58,159 --> 00:04:02,080
intelligible.

93
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:04,159
All through the discourse, I have tried

94
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:06,159
to illustrate whatever points I have

95
00:04:04,159 --> 00:04:08,640
made with parallel examples from

96
00:04:06,159 --> 00:04:10,239
European history and literature,

97
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:12,000
believing that these will aid in

98
00:04:10,239 --> 00:04:14,879
bringing the subject nearer to the

99
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,880
comprehension of foreign readers. Should

100
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:18,959
any of my illusions to religious

101
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:21,600
subjects and to religious workers be

102
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:23,919
