00:08:35,519 --> 00:08:40,680
Bushido, the soul of Japan by Inazonito.

204
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:49,360
Chapter 1. Bushido as an ethical system.

205
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:51,519
Chivalry is a flower no less indigenous

206
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:54,560
to the soil of Japan than its emblem,

207
00:08:51,519 --> 00:08:56,959
the cherry blossom. Nor is it a dried up

208
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:59,839
specimen of an antique virtue preserved

209
00:08:56,959 --> 00:09:02,080
in the herbarium of our history.

210
00:08:59,839 --> 00:09:04,720
It is still a living object of power and

211
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:07,760
beauty among us. And if it assumes no

212
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:10,080
tangible shape or form, it not the less

213
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:12,320
sense the moral atmosphere and makes us

214
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:15,440
aware that we are still under its potent

215
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:18,399
spell. The conditions of society which

216
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:20,959
brought it forth and nourished it have

217
00:09:18,399 --> 00:09:23,760
long disappeared. But as those faroff

218
00:09:20,959 --> 00:09:26,480
stars which once were and are not still

219
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:28,640
continue to shed their rays upon us, so

220
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:31,360
the light of chivalry which was a child

221
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:34,880
of feudalism still illuminates our moral

222
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:37,360
path surviving its mother institution.

223
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:39,920
It is a pleasure to me to reflect upon

224
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:41,920
this subject in the language of Burke

225
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:44,399
who uttered the well-known touching

226
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:46,880
eulogy over the neglected buyer of its

227
00:09:44,399 --> 00:09:49,760
European prototype.

228
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:52,640
It argues a sad defect of information

229
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:54,959
concerning the Far East when so eruded a

230
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:58,240
scholar as Dr. George Miller did not

231
00:09:54,959 --> 00:10:00,880
hesitate to affirm that chivalry or any

232
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:02,959
other similar institution has never

233
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:06,399
existed either among the nations of

234
00:10:02,959 --> 00:10:08,880
antiquity or among the modern orientals.

235
00:10:06,399 --> 00:10:11,360
Such ignorance, however, is amply

236
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:13,600
excusable as the third edition of the

237
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:15,920
good doctor's work appeared the same

238
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:18,880
year that Commodora Perry was knocking

239
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:21,360
at the portals of our exclusivism.

240
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:23,279
More than a decade later, about the time

241
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:26,560
that our feudalism was in the last

242
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:29,600
throws of existence, Karl Marx writing

243
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:32,079
his capital called the attention of his

244
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:34,079
readers to the peculiar advantage of

245
00:10:32,079 --> 00:10:37,279
studying the social and political

246
00:10:34,079 --> 00:10:40,640
institutions of feudalism as then to be

247
00:10:37,279 --> 00:10:42,399
seen in living form only in Japan. I

248
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:44,640
would likewise invite the western

249
00:10:42,399 --> 00:10:46,720
historical and ethical student to the

250
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:48,240
study of chivalry in the Japan of the

251
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:50,720
present.

252
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:53,040
Enticing as is a historical disquisition

253
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:55,920
on the comparison between European and

254
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:58,000
Japanese feudalism and chivalry, it is

255
00:10:55,920 --> 00:11:00,959
not the purpose of this paper to enter

256
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:04,399
into it at length. My attempt is rather

257
00:11:00,959 --> 00:11:08,160
to relate firstly the origin and sources

258
00:11:04,399 --> 00:11:10,880
of our chivalry, secondly its character

259
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:14,240
and teaching, thirdly its influence

260
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:16,160
among the masses, and fourthly the

261
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:17,760
continuity and permanence of its

262
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:20,240
influence.

263
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:22,880
Of these several points, the first will

264
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:24,640
be only brief and cursory, or else I

265
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:27,519
should have to take my readers into the

266
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:29,680
devious paths of our national history.

267
00:11:27,519 --> 00:11:32,079
The second will be dwelt upon at greater

268
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:34,160
length as being most likely to interest

269
00:11:32,079 --> 00:11:36,640
students of international ethics and

270
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:38,880
comparative ethology in our ways of

271
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:41,440
thought and action and the rest will be

272
